          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.5 How can Water be Evaporated Faster or Slower?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.147,
            0.743,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In section 8.1, we have learnt about evaporation. Let us explore it more!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.188,
            0.744,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe your surroundings. What are the conditions that affect how fast water evaporates? What differences do you see in evaporation on a cold day versus a hot day? Discuss with your friends. The following words may help in your discussion—fan, drying cloth, sweating, windy day, hot day, rainy day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.311,
            0.743,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us perform Activity 8.7 to investigate conditions that will affect how fast water will evaporate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.363,
            0.447,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 8.7: Let us investigate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.395,
            0.744,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take water in a small cap of a bottle (you may use sanitiser in place of water)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.442,
            0.744,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take the same amount of water in a plate. The exposed area of water in the bottle cap and the plate are different."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.489,
            0.535,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Keep both of them near each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.515,
            0.744,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Record the time taken for the water to completely evaporate in each case in Table 8.4."
